WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:15.532
Vinnie and Mandy followed Leo out of the workshop and into the streets of Florence.

2
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:19.687
"Wow!" gasped Mandy.

3
00:00:19.688 --> 00:00:23.405
Women dressed in long gowns passed by.

4
00:00:23.406 --> 00:00:28.488
Silver and gold nets held their hair away from their faces.

5
00:00:28.489 --> 00:00:33.945
Men wearing leather shoes and hats bowed as the women passed.

6
00:00:33.946 --> 00:00:36.990
"What a beautiful building!"

7
00:00:36.991 --> 00:00:40.180
Mandy pointed across the street.

8
00:00:40.181 --> 00:00:46.680
"That was designed by one of Florence's most famous architects," began Leo.

9
00:00:46.681 --> 00:00:50.769
Then he described everything about the building.

10
00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:55.704
"You sure do know a lot about architecture," said Vinnie.

11
00:00:55.705 --> 00:00:59.953
"I like to learn about everything," Leo replied.

12
00:00:59.954 --> 00:01:05.279
"By the way, thank you for helping us in there," said Mandy.

13
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.004
"Your teacher looked a little angry."

14
00:01:09.005 --> 00:01:11.199
Leo shrugged.

15
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.681
"No need to thank me.

16
00:01:13.682 --> 00:01:17.449
You guys were just lucky I found you first."

17
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.898
They walked down the street in silence.

18
00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:25.420
Mandy noticed two men arguing with a young woman.

19
00:01:25.421 --> 00:01:28.979
She asked Leo what was going on.

20
00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:33.195
"Those men are angry about her dress," he said.

21
00:01:33.196 --> 00:01:36.569
"Clothing is very important in Florence.

22
00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.645
Her dress has stripes on the sleeves.

23
00:01:39.646 --> 00:01:44.677
Women of her lower class are not allowed to wear stripes by law."

24
00:01:44.678 --> 00:01:49.037
"What?" asked Mandy, shocked.

25
00:01:49.038 --> 00:01:55.204
"There are strict rules about what people can and cannot wear," continued Leo.

26
00:01:55.205 --> 00:02:00.038
"Do you mean poor people cannot wear certain clothing?"

27
00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:04.580
asked Mandy, getting upset about the unfairness.

28
00:02:04.581 --> 00:02:08.091
"Naturally," replied Leo.

29
00:02:08.092 --> 00:02:13.406
"For example, only the wealthy can wear velvet and use gold thread."

30
00:02:13.407 --> 00:02:16.577
"But—," began Mandy.

31
00:02:16.578 --> 00:02:18.853
Vinnie interrupted.

32
00:02:18.854 --> 00:02:23.855
"Hey Mandy, everyone is singing as they work," he said.

33
00:02:23.856 --> 00:02:30.187
Sure enough, in almost every shop, people were singing or humming.

34
00:02:30.188 --> 00:02:36.041
"Yes. It is our custom to sing as much as possible!" said Leo.

35
00:02:36.042 --> 00:02:40.347
As they passed a barber shop, the owner came out.

36
00:02:40.348 --> 00:02:43.927
He was a bald man with a big stomach.

37
00:02:43.928 --> 00:02:47.147
He smiled when he saw Leo.

38
00:02:47.148 --> 00:02:50.096
"How are you?" he cried.

39
00:02:50.097 --> 00:02:52.957
He patted the boy on the back.

40
00:02:52.958 --> 00:02:56.271
"Is your back tooth bothering you again?

41
00:02:56.272 --> 00:02:58.678
I can pull it for you!"

42
00:02:58.679 --> 00:03:03.541
"I'm fine, Signori Fontana," replied Leo.

43
00:03:03.542 --> 00:03:08.484
"When are you coming for a trim?" asked Mr. Fontana.

44
00:03:08.485 --> 00:03:10.985
Mandy looked inside.

45
00:03:10.986 --> 00:03:16.718
A man was sitting in a big wooden chair, waiting to get his hair cut.

46
00:03:16.719 --> 00:03:20.856
"Soon, I promise," said Leo.

47
00:03:20.857 --> 00:03:28.209
"Bring me one of your magnificent drawings when you come, will you?" the man laughed.

48
00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:32.070
He waved and went back inside the shop.

49
00:03:32.071 --> 00:03:37.399
"Your barber pulls teeth?" asked Mandy, surprised.

50
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:45.355
"Of course, Signori Fontana also is the best surgeon in Florence," Leo replied.

51
00:03:45.356 --> 00:03:48.451
They stopped on top of a bridge.

52
00:03:48.452 --> 00:03:54.067
"This is the Ponte Vecchio, or the old bridge," explained Leo.

53
00:03:54.068 --> 00:03:57.726
"It's one of six bridges in Florence."

54
00:03:57.727 --> 00:04:01.897
The bridge was supported by three wide arches.

55
00:04:01.898 --> 00:04:07.946
Shops selling meat, fruits, and flowers lined the road over the bridge.

56
00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:11.442
Below, the river flowed calmly.

57
00:04:11.443 --> 00:04:16.667
"It is one of the most beautiful places in Florence," said Leo.

58
00:04:16.668 --> 00:04:22.247
The children agreed.
